    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d227">

                <pb facs="0344" n="232" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg232"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 818.00/320</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-03T14:00:00-05:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 3, 1918, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Arrests of civilians continue. Tinoco has been warned by Chamorro of danger to be
                    expected by way of Rio Frio and has dispatched more troops to Limon. Tinoco much
                    alarmed; expecting early outbreak of movement referred to in my January 25, 9
                        a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d227-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
